alyssa: FYI support flagged a customer flow where repeated 429s during a context-heavy embeddings migration caused the UI to render nonsense after automatic trimming. Our error-ref has guidance but no ready SDK snippet. Can someone add a tiny example + a short runbook?

tom: I can do a minimal JS + Python pair. Keep each ~6 lines showing: catch 429, trim, fallback model, record telemetry.

nora: Make sure we call out when NOT to auto-downgrade (legal/safety) and suggest a single retry only. Also add a Console tag example: event `client.retry` with `retry_reason` and `fallback_model`.

tom: Draft JS (compact):
```js
try {
  const r = await client.generate({model: 'redwood-large-v1', prompt: bigPrompt, max_tokens:1024})
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof RateLimitError) {
    client.metrics.increment('client.retry', {retry_reason: 'context_trim'})
    const short = trimContext(bigPrompt, 2048)
    await client.generate({model: 'redwood-small-v1', prompt: short, max_tokens:256})
  }
}
```

alyssa: Nice. Add one-line backoff note (exponential, cap 3s) in the JS comment so frontends can optionally show "degraded" banner on fallback.

tom: Added comment and one-paragraph blurb about quality vs cost/latency and a callout: "Do not auto-downgrade for regulated outputs".

docs-bot: Lint OK. Link scanner warns about a draft relative link; suggested replacement /error-reference/429.

nora: I'll update the migration guide with a single sentence showing the Console event and tags to help customers map alerts.

alyssa: Can someone add a changelog line once merged? "Add 429+context-trim runbook and minimal SDK fallback snippets (JS/Python)".

tom: Opening PR now and will include both snippets + 5-bullet runbook. https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/912

alyssa: Thanks — approving after PR lands. We'll monitor Console fallback_rate and iterate.
